{
  "slug": "almanax-security",
  "name": "Almanax Security",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Scan Git commits for security vulnerabilities using Almanax directly from Claude Code. The plugin connects to the Almanax MCP server to analyze commit diffs, surface findings by severity, and help you fix issues — all without leaving your terminal. Includes guided setup and support for scanning individual commits or commit ranges.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (2): `scan-commit` (Use Almanax to scan a Git commit diff for vulnerabilities and then summarize or fix the resulting findings), `setup` (Connect Claude Code to Almanax and walk the user through getting an API key from the Almanax web…)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `almanax`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install almanax-security@claude-community` from `almanax-ai/almanax-security-plugin` (`plugins/almanax-security`).",
